From: echo-penguin
Subject: [PATCH] fbcon: start rotated 90 degrees clockwise on cronos

The cronos panel is 480x960 portrait, mounted sideways. fbcon=rotate:1 would turn the text, but
the bootloader passes a command line of ~1012 bytes against a 1024-byte limit, and the extra
bytes hang the unit at the boot logo on a warm reboot (measured 2026-10-31). Make clockwise
the default instead; fbcon=rotate: still overrides it.
---
diff --git a/drivers/video/console/fbcon.c b/drivers/video/console/fbcon.c
index 510bc3f51dc..2e45e32657a 100644
--- a/drivers/video/console/fbcon.c
+++ b/drivers/video/console/fbcon.c
@@ -129,7 +129,12 @@ static char fontname[40];
 static int info_idx = -1;
 
 /* console rotation */
-static int initial_rotation;
+/*
+ * echo-penguin: the cronos panel is portrait, mounted sideways; start rotated 90 degrees clockwise
+ * so text reads in landscape without fbcon=rotate:1 (the bootloader's command line is near its
+ * 1024-byte limit, and a longer one hangs the unit on a warm reboot).
+ */
+static int initial_rotation = FB_ROTATE_CW;
 static int fbcon_has_sysfs;
 
 static const struct consw fb_con;
